   "spoken": "If a pawn lunges to attack the knight, resist the knee-jerk retreat — capture on e6 and hit back, or go further and sacrifice: leave the knight en prise, play into d4 and then take on c6, hitting queen and pawn at once. The piece is given up for a raging attack — and an attack like that is exactly what compensation means.",
