   "spoken": "But there was an in-between check on c1 that had to be dealt with first — and once the check is answered, the rook is no longer hanging, so the bishop can be taken after all. The pin evaporated because the tempo was spent elsewhere. The lesson: always check for the opponent's checks before trusting a pin.",
