   "t": 1442.5,
   "fen": "b2r2k1/p2n1R1p/1prN1np1/3p4/8/1P4P1/PB1R1PBP/6K1 w - - 1 24",
   "line": [
    "Rc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "This is exactly that flimsiness in action: a knight defends a rook while the knight itself is attacked and undefended. Move the knight and the rook drops; move the rook and the knight drops. A structure held together by a single thread never ends well.",
