   "line": [
    "Rfxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Blockade the isolated pawn with a rook and the opponent's whole army gets chained to defending it, which frees a free hand on the other wing. From there it's textbook conversion: use the kingside pawn majority to manufacture a passed pawn, and better still a protected passed pawn — the ideal, because it can never be attacked. March the king up, keep dropping the bishop back to harass the pawn so the enemy pieces are forever herded backward, and the protected passer ends up guarding the very square that delivers mate. Even in the endgame a careless king walk gets checkmated — activity never stops mattering."
