   "spoken": "A shortcut for judging whether a pin is dangerous: is there a pawn protecting the pinned piece? If a pawn shields it, there's little to fear. If nothing but the queen holds it, the pin bites — the moment pressure piles onto the pinned piece, it becomes very hard to defend.",
